{
  "identifier": "bioportal-gro_x2",
  "title": "Gene Regulation Ontology",
  "description": {
    "en": "The Gene Regulation Ontology (GRO) is a conceptual model for the domain of gene regulation. It covers processes  that are linked to the regulation of gene expression as well as physical entities that are involved in these processes (such as genes and transcription factors) in terms of ontology classes and semantic relations between classes."
